          { q: "What’s the difference between managed and self-serve networks?", a: "A managed network (like OKAD’s) handles everything: creator matching, brief distribution, quality control, revisions, and payments. A self-serve platform gives you a directory of creators, but you do all the operational work yourself. Managed costs more per video but saves 80%+ of internal time." },
